# Chaos: softer motion of the floating damage numbers (O215; client/BASE.md "0134"; src/client/chaostextmotion.h (new, pure),
# animatedtext.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0133).
# The stock number rises on a straight line, shows at full size at once and fades on a straight line (patches 0081 and 0100
# only shift it, scale its speed and give it a drift). With the new switch the same AnimatedText::drawText does this instead:
#  * pop: the text starts at 75% size, grows to 130% in the first 8% of its life and settles to 100% by 24% (a queued text is
#    scaled around its own centre with DrawQueue::setScale, the call the boss scale of patch 0020 uses; one condition per
#    number only while the pop runs);
#  * ease-out rise: the rise (the stock 48 px, the diagonal of GameDiagonalAnimatedText, or the Lua drift of patch 0100) follows
#    1 - (1 - u)^3 instead of u: quick at the start, slow at the end;
#  * smooth fade: smoothstep from the existing fade start (setFadeStart, stock 1/1.2) to the end of the life;
#  * sideways spread: every text gets a number from a counter and moves up to 8 px sideways by golden-ratio steps (Fibonacci
#    hashing), opening up with the rise, so numbers of one hit that appear one after the other land far apart (any six in a row
#    are 0.1 of the range apart at least). It adds to the random shift of game_damagescatter, which stays the Lua side.
# All the maths is in chaostextmotion.h (pure, tested by client/tools/chaostextmotion_test.cpp); drawText only calls it. The
# cost is a few float operations per visible text per frame and, for the first fifth of its life, one scale condition.
#  * AnimatedText.setSoftMotion(bool) / isSoftMotion() (static, one switch for all texts; default off in the engine, the overlay
#    module game_visualfx turns it on from the option). With it off the old code path runs unchanged.
#  * dataset.lua: option `numberMotion` (default on); its apply tells game_visualfx (`onOption('numberMotion', value)`).
#  * options/graphics.otui: a ninth checkbox "Soft damage numbers" under "Soft glow" (the panel grows from 162 to 181 px).
# Checked: applies after 0001-0133 on the base tree; the touched .cpp files pass g++ -fsyntax-only; the header passes its test.
# Not built, linked or run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
